# The trial of pod-acme in podssh (T-034; call C601), at podssh's main
# b9c04657 (pod-acme.commit), where podssh froze src/acme/ for the move
# (PodUtils/podssh#248, PodUtils/podssh@T-684), after the patch of
# pod-transit (pod-acme.needs), which moves each podcrates tag to v0.49.0.
# podssh-cli's acme/mod.rs becomes glue over pod-acme: it re-exports the
# crate and keeps `new` (podssh's HTTPS client through HTTPS_PROXY, the
# trust, the places of its cache, the refusal of PODSSH_CACHE_DIR=none and
# its exit codes), `keep` (the lines to the role's sender) and `Say`. The
# Pinggy road and the OpenTunnel road take Key and the CSR of a tunnel from
# the crate. The tests of the module leave podssh; its Pebble interop
# stays, as it runs the binary. The record with its citations, the
# repository checks; no moved file stays; the build; pod-acme in the tree;
# clippy and the tests of the CLI's role and of its node of the publish
# road; the Pebble interop of the binary; rustfmt of the crate that the
# patch changes; each test target that the gate names.
cargo run -q -p podssh-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podssh-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-repo.py
test "$(ls crates/podssh-cli/src/acme)" = mod.rs
cargo build -q
cargo tree -q -p podssh-cli -i pod-acme | grep -q '^pod-acme v'
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-cli -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --lib -- acme relay_serve:: pinggy_cert node_opentunnel
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --test relay_serve
sh scripts/interop-acme.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/debug/podssh"
cargo fmt -p podssh-cli --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-tests.py"
